    "title": "European Court Rules Against Russia Twice | NTD",
    "text": "Judges at Europe’s top human rights court ruled against Russia for both the Ukraine War and the 2014 downing of flight MH-17.\nIt’s the first time Russia was found to be a human rights violator since the 2022 Ukraine war began, and it’s the first time a court ruled on the flight tragedy.\nThere are a total of four cases the European Court of Human Rights will rule on. They are all brought forth by Ukraine and the Netherlands against Russia.\nIn 2014, a flight over a Russian separatist-controlled region of Ukraine was shot down. The flight was traveling from the Netherlands to Malaysia. All 298 people on board were killed after the Boeing 777 jet was struck by a Russian-made missile.",
